{"resource":{"id":"go-pdf-notes","title":"Go — PDF Notes","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"52 min","pages":106,"lastUpdated":"October 2026","tags":["Programming","Go","Concurrency"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Chapter-wise Go notes formatted for offline study — syntax, diagrams, interview call-outs, and revision summaries across the whole language."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"c1","label":"1. Introduction"},{"id":"c2","label":"2. Variables"},{"id":"c3","label":"3. Functions"},{"id":"c4","label":"4. Structs"},{"id":"c5","label":"5. Interfaces"},{"id":"c6","label":"6. Packages"},{"id":"c7","label":"7. Goroutines"},{"id":"c8","label":"8. Channels"},{"id":"c9","label":"9. HTTP"},{"id":"c10","label":"10. Databases"},{"id":"c11","label":"11. Testing"},{"id":"c12","label":"12. Deployment"},{"id":"review","label":"PDF Review"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Go — Quick Revision Notes","tag":"Programming","time":"6 min"},{"title":"Go — Cheat Sheet","tag":"Programming","time":"5 min"},{"title":"Go — Complete Tutorial","tag":"Programming","time":"55 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Own a comprehensive Go reference formatted for print.</li>\n          <li>Study each topic with syntax, examples, and interview call-outs.</li>\n          <li>Use comparison tables to solidify decisions (slice vs array, channel vs mutex).</li>\n          <li>Follow chapter summaries for rapid revision.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Introduction</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><strong>What is Go?</strong> A statically typed, compiled language designed by Google for large-scale backend software. Its trademarks are simplicity, fast compilation, and built-in concurrency.</p>\n        <p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> powers Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, and huge parts of modern cloud infrastructure.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Go's role in modern cloud infrastructure: containers, orchestration, and networked services.\" />\n        <p class=\"mt-2\"><strong>Chapter summary:</strong> Go trades feature count for readability; the standard library is the framework.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Variables</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>var name string = &quot;Ada&quot;\nage := 30\nconst Pi = 3.14</code></pre></div>\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Form</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Use</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\"><code>var</code></td><td class=\"p-2\">Explicit type or zero value</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\"><code>:=</code></td><td class=\"p-2\">Inside functions; type inferred</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\"><code>const</code></td><td class=\"p-2\">Compile-time constants</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <p><strong>Interview note:</strong> unused variables are compile errors — a core language design decision.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Functions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>func swap(a, b int) (int, int) { return b, a }\nfunc divide(a, b float64) (float64, error) { /* ... */ }</code></pre></div>\n        <p>Named returns, variadic parameters, first-class functions, and closures are all supported.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Structs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>type User struct {\n  ID   int\n  Name string\n}</code></pre></div>\n        <p><strong>Best practice:</strong> keep struct fields sorted by size to minimise padding.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Interfaces</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Small interfaces beat large ones. The standard library uses <code>io.Reader</code>, <code>io.Writer</code>, <code>fmt.Stringer</code> — one or two methods each.</p>\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Language</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Interface style</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Java</td><td class=\"p-2\">Explicit <code>implements</code></td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">Go</td><td class=\"p-2\">Implicit satisfaction</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Packages</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Package layout: <code>cmd/</code> for main packages, <code>internal/</code> for private code, <code>pkg/</code> for reusable libraries.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Goroutines</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Cheap to create (a few KB stack, growing dynamically). Multiplexed onto OS threads by the runtime scheduler.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-red-500/40 bg-red-500/10 text-red-900 dark:text-red-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z\"/><path d=\"M12 9v4\"/><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Leaking goroutines</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Every launched goroutine must have a defined exit path — otherwise you leak memory.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Channels</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>ch := make(chan int, 4)\nch &lt;- 1\nv, ok := &lt;-ch // ok is false when closed and empty\nclose(ch)</code></pre></div>\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Kind</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Behaviour</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Unbuffered</td><td class=\"p-2\">Send blocks until receive</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">Buffered</td><td class=\"p-2\">Send blocks only when full</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. HTTP</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><code>net/http</code> is production-grade. Prefer explicit servers over the default mux in real services.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Typical Go service architecture: handler → service → repository → database, wrapped in middleware.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Databases</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Use <code>database/sql</code> with a driver (<code>pgx</code>, <code>mysql</code>). Always pass <code>context.Context</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Testing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Table-driven tests are the community standard. Run with <code>-race</code> and <code>-cover</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"c12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">12. Deployment</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Build a static binary, ship it in a <em>distroless</em> or <em>scratch</em> container, expose health endpoints, and emit structured logs.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"review\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">PDF Review</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold\">Revision Notes</h3>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Goroutines + channels &gt; threads + locks for most Go workloads.</li>\n          <li>Errors are values — wrap with <code>%w</code>.</li>\n          <li>Interfaces are satisfied implicitly.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Self Assessment</h3>\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Write a table test for a pure function.</li>\n          <li>Explain the memory model in 3 sentences.</li>\n          <li>Sketch a producer/consumer pipeline with channels.</li>\n        </ol>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Important Topics</h3>\n        <p>Concurrency, error handling, interfaces, and context propagation — the most common interview and code-review themes.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Can I use this offline?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes — use the Download PDF / Print button in the toolbar.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is Go a functional language?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No, but it supports first-class functions and closures.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Zero value</strong> — the default for every type (<code>0</code>, <code>\"\"</code>, <code>nil</code>).</li>\n          <li><strong>Composition</strong> — building types by embedding rather than inheriting.</li>\n          <li><strong>Vendoring</strong> — copying dependencies into your repo for reproducible builds.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n          Study notes for educational use. Always consult go.dev and official library docs for\n          authoritative information. Trademarks belong to their respective owners.\n        </p>\n      </div></section>"}